IMPORT prelude

-- Registration of Deeds Act 1988 (Singapore) -- searches, evidence, rectification, leases, offences, service:
-- ss 17 to 28 and 30.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Registration of Deeds Act 1988 -- searches, rectification, offences`

§§ `17 -- registering in order of presentation`

-- s 17(1): the Registrar "must register all assurances and other instruments that are entitled to be registered ...
-- in the order in which they are so presented".
-- s 17(2): an assurance or instrument "must not be registered under this Act unless it complies with the
-- requirements of this Act and the rules."
GIVEN `presented at` IS A NUMBER, `other presented at` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must deal with the first before the second` IF
    `presented at` LESS THAN `other presented at`

GIVEN `complies with the Act and the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument may be registered` IF
    `complies with the Act and the rules`

§§ `18 to 22 -- searches and what can be proved by the register`

-- s 18: any person may inspect and search the public records, on days and hours the Registrar appoints and on paying
-- the fee. s 19: an official search is required by a signed written requisition specifying the Government survey lot
-- number and the mukim or town subdivision number, and either (a) specified instruments or (b) a PERIOD commencing
-- with a specified instrument that "does not exceed the statutory period of limitation for title to be deduced under
-- the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886". The certificate is signed and sealed and "receivable in evidence".
DECLARE Requisition HAS
    `signed in writing by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the survey lot number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the mukim or town subdivision number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies the instruments or a period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period exceeds the statutory period for deducing title` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the requisition` IS A Requisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requisition is valid` IF
        `the requisition`'s `signed in writing by the person`
    AND `the requisition`'s `specifies the survey lot number`
    AND `the requisition`'s `specifies the mukim or town subdivision number`
    AND `the requisition`'s `specifies the instruments or a period`
    AND NOT `the requisition`'s `the period exceeds the statutory period for deducing title`

-- s 21(2): a certified copy is receivable as evidence of the contents. s 21(3): it does NOT dispense with production of
-- an original where that would otherwise be required, nor with proof of due making and execution.
-- s 22: a print-out of a public record stored in a computer, certified a true reproduction, is receivable in evidence.
GIVEN `the original is otherwise required to be produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certified copy dispenses with the original` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the certified copy proves due execution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certified copy proves that the original was duly made and executed` IF
    FALSE

§§ `23 -- fiduciaries who rely on a certificate`

-- s 23: a solicitor, trustee, executor, agent or other person in a fiduciary position who obtains (a) a certificate of
-- the result of an official search, or (b) a certified copy of or extract from a document or entry, "is not answerable
-- for any loss, damage or injury that arises from any error in that certificate, copy or extract."
-- The protection is unqualified by good faith or reasonable care.
DECLARE Fiduciary IS ONE OF
    `a solicitor`
    `a trustee`
    `an executor`
    `an agent`
    `another person in a fiduciary position`
    `a person not in a fiduciary position`

DECLARE Document IS ONE OF
    `a certificate of an official search`
    `a certified copy or extract`
    `an informal note of an oral enquiry`

GIVEN `who relied` IS A Fiduciary, `on what` IS A Document
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is protected from liability for an error in the document` IF
        (CONSIDER `who relied`
            WHEN `a person not in a fiduciary position` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND (CONSIDER `on what`
            WHEN `an informal note of an oral enquiry` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE)

§§ `24 -- rectification of the register`

-- s 24(1): "Any person claiming any estate or interest in any land within Singapore may AT ANY TIME apply to the
-- General Division of the High Court" for an order that the register be rectified, an entry made or cancelled, a
-- certificate amended or cancelled, a document produced, or priority suspended pending proceedings.
-- s 24(2): the application must be served on the Registrar of Titles where it affects proprietorship, description or
-- area of land comprised in a Land Titles Act certificate of title.
-- s 24(3): the court may refuse or, if satisfied of the justice of the case, make such order as is just and expedient.
-- s 24(5): appeal within the prescribed time.
-- s 24(7): a person who has custody of an instrument subject to such an order and "refuses or neglects to produce"
-- it to the Registrar "shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 2 YEARS". No fine is provided.
DECLARE RectificationApplication HAS
    `the applicant claims an estate or interest in land within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter affects land comprised in a Land Titles Act certificate of title` IS A BOOLEAN
    `served on the Registrar of Titles` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied of the justice of the case` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A RectificationApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may apply for rectification` IF
    `the application`'s `the applicant claims an estate or interest in land within Singapore`

GIVEN `the application` IS A RectificationApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application must also be served on the Registrar of Titles` IF
    `the application`'s `the matter affects land comprised in a Land Titles Act certificate of title`

GIVEN `the application` IS A RectificationApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application is properly served` IF
        NOT `the application must also be served on the Registrar of Titles` `the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `served on the Registrar of Titles`

-- The Act sets no time limit on an application.
GIVEN `years since the entry was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an application is out of time` IF
    FALSE

DECLARE ProductionOffence HAS
    `the person has custody of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a rectification order covers the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar required production` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person refused or neglected to produce it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A ProductionOffence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the production offence` IF
        `the facts`'s `the person has custody of the instrument`
    AND `the facts`'s `a rectification order covers the instrument`
    AND `the facts`'s `the Registrar required production`
    AND `the facts`'s `the person refused or neglected to produce it`

-- Maximum term, in years.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment for the production offence` MEANS 2

-- A fine is not provided as a penalty at all.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the production offence carries a fine` IF
    FALSE

§§ `25 -- short leases`

-- s 25(1): "Nothing in this Act extends to any lease for a term not exceeding 7 years or any assignment thereof where
-- accompanied by ACTUAL POSSESSION from the making of the lease or assignment."
-- s 25(2): for deciding whether an instrument may be registered, (a) "the right or option to extend the term of a lease
-- for any further period granted by the lessor to the lessee is deemed to be part of the term of years granted by the
-- lease"; and (b) "no account is to be taken of the fact that the lease may be determined on the happening of an event".
-- And s 2(1): "lease" includes an agreement for a lease.
--
-- So a 5-year lease with possession and an option to renew for 3 more is an 8-year lease and is not excluded; a
-- 7-year lease without actual possession is not excluded; and a 10-year lease terminable on 6 months' notice is a
-- 10-year lease.
DECLARE LeaseFacts HAS
    `the term in years` IS A NUMBER
    `the longest extension the lessee has the right or option to take, in years` IS A NUMBER
    `accompanied by actual possession from the making` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it can be determined earlier on an event` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an agreement for a lease` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the lease` IS A LeaseFacts
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term counted for section 25` MEANS
    `the lease`'s `the term in years` PLUS `the lease`'s `the longest extension the lessee has the right or option to take, in years`

GIVEN `the lease` IS A LeaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is outside the Act` IF
        `the term counted for section 25` `the lease` AT MOST 7
    AND `the lease`'s `accompanied by actual possession from the making`

GIVEN `the lease` IS A LeaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is within the Act` IF
    NOT `the lease is outside the Act` `the lease`

-- A power to terminate early is ignored in measuring the term.
GIVEN `the lease` IS A LeaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an early determination right shortens the term counted` IF
    FALSE

-- s 29(1)(h) lets the Authority exempt leases OVER 7 years by rules. None were retrieved.

§§ `26 -- the Registrar's wilful misconduct`

-- s 26: the Registrar or any person employed under the Registrar who "wilfully neglects his or her duty ... or wilfully
-- commits or suffers to be committed any undue or fraudulent practice in the execution of that office, intending
-- thereby to cause or knowing it to be likely that he or she may thereby cause injury as defined in the Penal Code 1871
-- to any person, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be punished on conviction with a fine or with imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 7 years or with both."
-- The fine has no stated maximum.
DECLARE RegistrarConduct HAS
    `the person is the Registrar or employed under the Registrar for the purposes of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wilfully neglected duty or wilfully committed or suffered an undue or fraudulent practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended injury or knew it likely` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A RegistrarConduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer commits the section 26 offence` IF
        `the conduct`'s `the person is the Registrar or employed under the Registrar for the purposes of the Act`
    AND `the conduct`'s `wilfully neglected duty or wilfully committed or suffered an undue or fraudulent practice`
    AND `the conduct`'s `intended injury or knew it likely`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment for the section 26 offence` MEANS 7

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 26 states a maximum fine` IF
    FALSE

§§ `27 -- offences by anyone`

-- s 27: a person who (a) intentionally makes a false statement, whether on oath or not, before an officer acting under
-- the Act; (b) fraudulently procures, assists in procuring, or is privy to the fraudulent procuring of any instrument or
-- entry or alteration; (c) intentionally delivers a false document to a registering officer; (d) knowingly misleads or
-- deceives any person authorised to demand an explanation or information about land or title; (e) falsely impersonates
-- another and in that character presents a document or makes a statement; (f) fraudulently removes records or defaces
-- them; or (g) abets an offence under the Act -- is liable to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding
-- 3 years or both.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `intentionally making a false statement before an officer, on oath or not`
    `fraudulently procuring an instrument or entry`
    `intentionally delivering a false document to a registering officer`
    `knowingly misleading a person authorised to demand an explanation`
    `falsely impersonating another to present a document`
    `fraudulently removing or defacing records`
    `abetting an offence under the Act`
    `carelessly making a false statement`
    `innocently presenting a document that turns out to be false`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a section 27 offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `carelessly making a false statement` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `innocently presenting a document that turns out to be false` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 27` MEANS 5000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment under section 27, in years` MEANS 3

§§ `28 -- fees`

-- s 28(1): the Registrar "is not required to do any act or permit any act to be done in respect of which any fee is
-- specified or fixed except on payment of that fee." Together with s 13(1)(d) this means fees are a condition both of
-- the Registrar acting and of registration.
GIVEN `a fee is specified for the act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must act` IF
    (NOT `a fee is specified for the act`) OR `the fee has been paid`

§§ `30 -- service of notices`

-- s 30(1): "Any notice required by this Act to be served on any person is deemed to be duly served on the person if
-- sent by registered post to the person's LAST KNOWN ADDRESS IN SINGAPORE despite the fact that it is returned through
-- the post as undelivered."
-- s 30(2): s 72 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 "does not apply to the service on a proprietor of a
-- notice under this Act."
--
-- s 8(2)(a) requires a caveat to state the parties' "addresses for the service of notices under this Act", but s 30
-- deems service at the LAST KNOWN ADDRESS IN SINGAPORE. A party whose stated address for service is abroad, or who has
-- no address in Singapore, is not within the deeming at all; and a letter sent to the stated address for service that
-- is not the last known Singapore address does not attract it either.
DECLARE Service HAS
    `sent by registered post` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sent to the person's last known address in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sent to the address for service stated in the caveat` IS A BOOLEAN
    `returned undelivered` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service is deemed effected` IF
        `the service`'s `sent by registered post`
    AND `the service`'s `sent to the person's last known address in Singapore`

§§ `31 -- old short leases`

-- s 31(3): "Any lease for a term exceeding 3 years but less than 7 years or any assignment thereof executed or made
-- before 30 November 1988 and which was not registered under the repealed [Act] may, despite section 25 of this Act, be
-- registered under this Act, and unless so registered is not admissible in any court as evidence of title to land."
--
-- s 31(3) is not limited to leases WITHOUT possession. A pre-1988 lease of 5 years with actual possession is outside the
-- Act by s 25 if made after 30 November 1988, but inadmissible as evidence of title unless registered if made before.
-- (A lease of exactly 7 years, or of exactly 3, is caught by neither branch of s 31(3).)
DECLARE OldLease HAS
    `term in years` IS A NUMBER
    `made before 30 November 1988` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered under the repealed Act or this Act` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the lease` IS AN OldLease
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 31(3) catches the lease` IF
        `the lease`'s `made before 30 November 1988`
    AND `the lease`'s `term in years` GREATER THAN 3
    AND `the lease`'s `term in years` LESS THAN 7

GIVEN `the lease` IS AN OldLease
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old lease is inadmissible as evidence of title` IF
        `section 31(3) catches the lease` `the lease`
    AND NOT `the lease`'s `registered under the repealed Act or this Act`
